## Teaching Tools

When logged into a verified teacher account, you have access to the AI Teaching Assistant, which can support lesson planning, assessment, classroom facilitation, and just-in-time teaching support throughout the unit.


<p style="font-size:14pt; margin-top:12px;">

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">

   <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;"> 🤖 AI Teaching Assistant</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px;">

</summary>

  <div style="margin-top:18px; background:#F5F7F8; border-radius:14px; padding:20px;">

  <div style="display:flex; gap:24px; align-items:flex-start; flex-wrap:wrap;">

  <div style="flex:1; min-width:260px;">

  <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.5;">
          <strong>AI Teaching Assistant</strong> is a support tool designed for computer science and AI educators. It helps teachers save time, assess student work, and get classroom support while teaching.
        </p>

  <ul style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.6; padding-left:20px;">
          <li>Instant rubric-aligned feedback</li>
          <li>Suggestions for differentiation and teaching strategies</li>
          <li>Lesson summaries and classroom support</li>
          <li>Reduced grading and prep time</li>
        </ul>

  <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.5;">
          The AI Teaching Assistant is available for verified teachers in the bottom-left corner of the screen.
        </p>

  <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.5; margin-top:18px;">
  🔗 
  <a href="https://code.org/en-US/artificial-intelligence/teaching-assistant" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-weight:bold;">
    Learn more about AI Teaching Assistant
  </a>
</p>

